From: meta-quantum-safe CI <ci@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 22 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: respect OPENSSL_MODULES_PATH override

Older oqs-provider releases (e.g. 0.6.1) unconditionally set
OPENSSL_MODULES_PATH based on the sysroot libcrypto path, which makes Yocto
installs land under sysroot-derived paths and prevents packaging.

Allow OPENSSL_MODULES_PATH to be overridden (as a CMake cache variable), and
only compute a default when it is not provided.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto-specific install path handling]

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 8d0b7b8..be5e3c1 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -64,7 +64,8 @@ cmake_path(APPEND OQS_MODULES_PARENT_PATH "ossl-modules" OUTPUT_VARIABLE OPENSSL_
 else()
 get_filename_component(OPENSSL_LIB_DIR ${OPENSSL_CRYPTO_LIBRARY} DIRECTORY)
-set(OPENSSL_MODULES_PATH ${OPENSSL_LIB_DIR}/ossl-modules)
+if(NOT DEFINED OPENSSL_MODULES_PATH)
+    set(OPENSSL_MODULES_PATH ${OPENSSL_LIB_DIR}/ossl-modules CACHE PATH "Path to OpenSSL modules")
+endif()
 endif()
 
 # Add required include for liboqs
-- 
